<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">blacksmithing</ansi> (skill)

Blacksmithing is the craft of working metal. With a forge and the right materials a
blacksmith can produce weapons, shields, and eventually armor. The skill is governed
by <ansi fg="yellow">Strength</ansi> — heavier work demands a stronger hand.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">forge</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             The Forge is east of Town Square in Startland.
  Materials: Iron ingots, leather strips, wooden planks, and similar raw materials.
             Find them on the ground in The Forge or loot cave goblins.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Iron Dagger</ansi>     Skill 0   1x iron-ingot, 1x leather-strip       3 rounds
  <ansi fg="yellow">Iron Buckler</ansi>    Skill 5   2x iron-ingot, 1x wooden-plank         4 rounds

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Blacksmithing improves through use. Each successful craft has a chance to advance your
skill. Because crafting happens infrequently compared to combat, the skill progresses
faster per use than combat skills do.

There is no trainer for blacksmithing — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including blacksmithing ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting a blacksmithing recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current blacksmithing skill level.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help craft</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help alchemy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>

